        def_en: "The enzyme catalysing the metabolically irreversible step that COMMITS glucose to glycolysis -- glucose 6-phosphate could still have gone to glycogen or the pentose phosphate pathway, but fructose 1,6-bisphosphate cannot. Regulated at several allosteric sites: inhibited by ATP (which is also one of its substrates, and its own end product), relieved by ADP and AMP, and inhibited more deeply when citrate is high. At physiological concentrations of all of these, however, it is virtually inactive without fructose 2,6-bisphosphate -- so the allosteric effectors are fine-tuning on top of that switch.",
        def_cn: "催化「把葡萄糖承诺给糖酵解」那个代谢上不可逆步骤的酶——glucose 6-phosphate 本来还可以去糖原或磷酸戊糖途径，而 fructose 1,6-bisphosphate 不能。它在若干别构位点上受调控：被 ATP 抑制（而 ATP 同时是它的底物之一、也是这条通路的终产物），被 ADP 和 AMP 解除抑制，在 citrate 高时抑制加深。但在这一切都处于生理浓度时，没有 fructose 2,6-bisphosphate 它几乎不活跃——所以这些别构效应物都是在那个开关之上做微调。"
