        def_en: "The central regulator of this section and the one the Czech textbook never mentions. It is NOT an intermediate of glycolysis or gluconeogenesis -- nothing flows through it; it exists purely to carry information. It activates PFK-1 by raising its affinity for fructose 6-phosphate and lowering its affinity for the inhibitors ATP and citrate, and simultaneously inhibits FBPase-1 by lowering its affinity for its substrate. The load-bearing fact: at physiological concentrations of everything else, PFK-1 is virtually inactive without it. Its level is set by the bifunctional PFK-2/FBPase-2 protein, which is where hormones act.",
        def_cn: "本节的核心调节物，也是捷克教材从未提及的那一个。它不是糖酵解或糖异生的中间物——没有任何物质流经它；它存在的唯一目的就是携带信息。它通过提高 PFK-1 对 fructose 6-phosphate 的亲和力、降低它对抑制剂 ATP 和 citrate 的亲和力来激活 PFK-1；同时通过降低 FBPase-1 对底物的亲和力来抑制它。承重的那个事实是：在其余一切都处于生理浓度时，没有它 PFK-1 几乎不活跃。它的水平由双功能的 PFK-2/FBPase-2 蛋白决定——而那正是激素下手的地方。"
