        def_en: "One polypeptide carrying two opposing enzymatic activities: PFK-2 makes fructose 2,6-bisphosphate from fructose 6-phosphate, FBPase-2 hydrolyses it away. Because both are on the same chain, ONE covalent modification changes both at once in opposite directions -- reciprocity built into the protein rather than maintained by regulation. Phosphorylation by cAMP-dependent protein kinase turns FBPase-2 up and PFK-2 down; dephosphorylation does the reverse. Do not confuse the pair with PFK-1/FBPase-1: the 1,6 pair carries metabolic traffic, the 2,6 pair carries a signal.",
        def_cn: "一条多肽上带着两个方向相反的酶活性：PFK-2 用 fructose 6-phosphate 造出 fructose 2,6-bisphosphate，FBPase-2 把它水解掉。因为两者在同一条链上，一次共价修饰就能同时把两者朝相反方向改变——「互反」被做进了蛋白里，而不是靠调控去维持。cAMP 依赖的蛋白激酶的磷酸化把 FBPase-2 调上去、把 PFK-2 调下来；去磷酸化则相反。不要把这一对与 PFK-1/FBPase-1 混淆：「1,6」那一对搬运代谢流量，「2,6」这一对搬运信号。"
