        def_en: "The four-step chain by which a hormone in the blood reaches an enzyme in the cytosol within seconds. Low blood glucose releases glucagon; glucagon stimulates liver adenylyl cyclase to make cyclic AMP from ATP; cAMP activates cAMP-dependent protein kinase (PKA); PKA phosphorylates the bifunctional PFK-2/FBPase-2 protein, raising FBPase-2 and lowering PFK-2, so fructose 2,6-bisphosphate falls, glycolysis is inhibited and gluconeogenesis stimulated. Insulin reverses it by stimulating a phosphoprotein phosphatase. No new protein is made anywhere in this chain, which is why it is called the rapid arm.",
        def_cn: "血中的一个激素在几秒内够到胞质中一个酶的那条四步链。低血糖 → 释放 glucagon → glucagon 刺激肝的 adenylyl cyclase 把 ATP 做成 cyclic AMP → cAMP 激活 cAMP 依赖的蛋白激酶（PKA）→ PKA 磷酸化双功能的 PFK-2/FBPase-2 蛋白，使 FBPase-2 升、PFK-2 降，于是 F2,6BP 下降，糖酵解被抑制、糖异生被刺激。Insulin 通过刺激一个磷酸蛋白磷酸酶把它逆转。这条链上任何一步都不需要新合成蛋白——这正是它被称作「快速臂」的原因。"
