        def_en: "The mitochondrial branch point where fat gets a vote on glucose. Pyruvate can go to acetyl-CoA (pyruvate dehydrogenase complex, feeding the citric acid cycle) or to oxaloacetate (pyruvate carboxylase, starting gluconeogenesis). Acetyl-CoA decides, acting on both branches in opposite directions: it is a POSITIVE allosteric modulator of pyruvate carboxylase and a NEGATIVE modulator of pyruvate dehydrogenase, the latter by stimulating a protein kinase that inactivates the complex. So when fatty acid breakdown floods the mitochondrion with acetyl-CoA, pyruvate is pushed towards glucose instead of towards more acetyl-CoA.",
        def_cn: "线粒体内那个「脂肪对葡萄糖投票」的分叉点。丙酮酸可以去 acetyl-CoA（经 pyruvate dehydrogenase 复合体，给柠檬酸循环供料），也可以去 oxaloacetate（经 pyruvate carboxylase，开启糖异生）。做决定的是 acetyl-CoA，它对两个分支的作用方向相反：它是 pyruvate carboxylase 的正性别构调节物，同时是 pyruvate dehydrogenase 的负性调节物（后者通过刺激一个使该复合体失活的蛋白激酶实现）。所以当脂肪酸分解把线粒体灌满 acetyl-CoA 时，丙酮酸被推向葡萄糖，而不是推向更多的 acetyl-CoA。"
